5. Compiler Fossil

The recurring pipeline is:

x
\xrightarrow{O}
o
\xrightarrow{D}
d
\xrightarrow{C}
z
\xrightarrow{T}
r
\xrightarrow{R}
\hat{x}
\xrightarrow{V}
s

where:

* O: observe.
* D: distill.
* C: compress.
* T: translate.
* R: reconstruct.
* V: validate.
* s: fidelity score.

The entire compiler is:

\mathcal{P}
=
V \circ R \circ T \circ C \circ D \circ O

The system should update itself when validation fails:

\theta_{t+1}
=
\theta_t
-
\eta
\nabla_\theta
D(x,\hat{x})

Here, \theta represents extraction rules, weights, mappings, or reconstruction procedures.

Pseudocode

FUNCTION PANTHEON_COMPILE(raw_input, target_medium):
    observation ← observe(raw_input)
    distilled ← distill(observation)
    seed ← compress(distilled)
    translated ← translate(seed, target_medium)
    reconstruction ← reconstruct(translated)
    score ← validate(raw_input, reconstruction)
    IF score < minimum_fidelity:
        seed ← repair_seed(
            seed,
            validation_errors
        )
    RETURN {
        observation,
        distilled,
        seed,
        translated,
        reconstruction,
        score
    }

